From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:52:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let a theme set the screensaver's names and screen shapes

The slideshow and video screensavers fitted every picture at its own
shape, so a TV game's 256x224 capture showed at 8:7 with black sides
while the rest of the interface showed TV systems at 4:3. Their names
were the system's full name in grey with a hard outline and no scrim,
and the game's name gave way to its marquee.

A menuScreenSaver element gives the game's and the system's names a
font and colour each, a scrim under them, names for systems instead
of their full names, and the systems whose pictures and videos take
the screen's 4:3 (3:4 upright). The game's name is then text, left
at the menus' row margin. Without the element nothing changes.
